  Description=COBOL PROGRAM
  Parameter=
</DATA>
<DATA=Code>
  2009-01-01 12:00  => IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* SSG-4 (MT-043): one CHABAN for every CHABAN and CHAB100 call.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* Builds records from the run's data images (input CHAIN, the
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* Accept file mapped by the skeleton hand-off). Card length,
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* output length and record counts come from SGSPARM; see
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* _scratch\spike-chaban\spec.md.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PROGRAM-ID. 'ASSURFED-UTILIT-CHABAN-GN'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => CONFIGURATION SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => SOURCE-COMPUTER. UNIVAC-1100-10.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => OBJECT-COMPUTER. UNIVAC-1100-10.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE-CONTROL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT PARMF ASSIGN TO DISC SGSPARM.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT FI1 ASSIGN TO DISC CHAIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT FO1 ASSIGN TO DISC CHAOUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DATA DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  PARMF
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  P-TYPE         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  P-REST         PIC X(78).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-FILE-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PF-NAME        PIC X(30).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PF-LEN         PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(43).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-NB-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PN-REC         PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PN-PER         PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(68).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  FI1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     RECORD VARYING IN SIZE FROM 1 TO 4001
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DEPENDING ON WS-IN-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  FI1-REC PIC X(4001).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  FO1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  FO1-REC PIC X(4000).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  RECIN              PIC X(4001).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  WS-REC             PIC X(4200).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  WS-IN-LEN          PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  P-CARD             PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 80.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  P-LEN              PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  N-REC              PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  N-PER              PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  R                  PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  C                  PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  KP                 PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  CP-LEN             PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  NB-CARDS           PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  NB-OUT             PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  DISPLAY-LINE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  DISP-MESSAGE   PIC X(24).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  DISP-CT        PIC Z(11)9.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PROCEDURE DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DEBUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT PARMF.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-LECT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ PARMF AT END GO TO PARM-FIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'IN'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PF-LEN TO P-CARD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'OU'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PF-LEN TO P-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'NB'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PN-REC TO N-REC
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PN-PER TO N-PER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO PARM-LECT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-FIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE PARMF.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT FI1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN OUTPUT FO1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 0 TO R.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => REC-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF R NOT < N-REC GO TO FINW.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO WS-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO KP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 0 TO C.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => CARD-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF C NOT < N-PER GO TO REC-WRITE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO RECIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ FI1 INTO RECIN AT END GO TO FINW.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO NB-CARDS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE WS-IN-LEN TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > P-CARD
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE P-CARD TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > 0
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE RECIN (1:CP-LEN) TO WS-REC (KP:CP-LEN).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD P-CARD TO KP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO C.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO CARD-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => REC-WRITE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE FO1-REC FROM WS-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO NB-OUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO R.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO REC-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FINW.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE '    DATA CARDS READ     ' TO DISP-MESSAGE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE NB-CARDS TO DISP-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DISPLAY DISPLAY-LINE UPON PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE '    RECORDS WRITTEN     ' TO DISP-MESSAGE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE NB-OUT TO DISP-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DISPLAY DISPLAY-LINE UPON PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE FI1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE FO1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     STOP RUN.
</DATA>
