<DATA=Code>
  2009-01-01 12:00  => IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* SSG-4 (MT-043): one FUSBA for every FUSBA and FUSBA2 call.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* Files, key fields, mode and field moves come from the SGSPARM
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* file written by the skeleton hand-off; see
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* _scratch\spike-fusba\spec.md. File 1 = update file, file 2 =
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* master. Modes: C split, D delete, U update, M update with
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* several masters per key (FUSBA2).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PROGRAM-ID. 'ASSURFED-UTILIT-FUSBA-GN'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => CONFIGURATION SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => SOURCE-COMPUTER. UNIVAC-1100-10.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => OBJECT-COMPUTER. UNIVAC-1100-10.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE-CONTROL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT PARMF ASSIGN TO DISC SGSPARM.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT FI1 ASSIGN TO DISC FUSIN1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT FI2 ASSIGN TO DISC FUSIN2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT FO1 ASSIGN TO DISC FUSOUT1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT FO2 ASSIGN TO DISC FUSOUT2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DATA DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  PARMF
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  P-TYPE         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  P-REST         PIC X(78).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-FILE-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PF-NAME        PIC X(30).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PF-LEN         PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(43).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-MODE-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PD-MODE        PIC X.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(77).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-KEY-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PK-POS         PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PK-LEN         PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(68).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-MOVE-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PM-IPOS        PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PM-ILEN        PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PM-OPOS        PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PM-OLEN        PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(58).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  FI1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     RECORD VARYING IN SIZE FROM 1 TO 4001
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DEPENDING ON WS-LEN1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  FI1-REC PIC X(4001).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  FI2
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     RECORD VARYING IN SIZE FROM 1 TO 4001
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DEPENDING ON WS-LEN2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  FI2-REC PIC X(4001).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  FO1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  FO1-REC PIC X(4000).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  FO2
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  FO2-REC PIC X(4000).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  RECIN              PIC X(4001).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  REC1               PIC X(4000).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  REC2               PIC X(4000).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  RECOUT             PIC X(4000).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  KEY1               PIC X(400).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  KEY2               PIC X(400).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PREV-KEY2          PIC X(400).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  WS-LEN1            PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  WS-LEN2            PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  P-LEN1             PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  P-LEN2             PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  N-IN               PIC 9(3) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  N-OUT              PIC 9(3) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  P-MODE             PIC X VALUE 'C'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  N-K1               PIC 9(3) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  N-K2               PIC 9(3) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  N-FM               PIC 9(3) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  I                  PIC 9(3) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  KP                 PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  KL                 PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  KL2                PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  CP-LEN             PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  TARGET             PIC 9 VALUE 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  EOF1               PIC X VALUE 'N'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  EOF2               PIC X VALUE 'N'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  NB-LUS1            PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  NB-LUS2            PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  NB-OUT1            PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  NB-OUT2            PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  NB-MAJ             PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  NB-DEL             PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  OUT-TAB.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  OUT-LEN        PIC 9(5) COMP OCCURS 2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  K1-TAB.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  K1-ENT OCCURS 20.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         05  K1-POS     PIC 9(5) COMP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         05  K1-LEN     PIC 9(5) COMP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  K2-TAB.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  K2-ENT OCCURS 20.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         05  K2-POS     PIC 9(5) COMP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         05  K2-LEN     PIC 9(5) COMP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  FM-TAB.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FM-ENT OCCURS 20.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         05  FM-IPOS    PIC 9(5) COMP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         05  FM-ILEN    PIC 9(5) COMP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         05  FM-OPOS    PIC 9(5) COMP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         05  FM-OLEN    PIC 9(5) COMP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  DISPLAY-LINE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  DISP-MESSAGE   PIC X(24).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  DISP-CT        PIC Z(11)9.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PROCEDURE DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DEBUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT PARMF.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-LECT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ PARMF AT END GO TO PARM-FIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'IN'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 1 TO N-IN
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        IF N-IN = 1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>           MOVE PF-LEN TO P-LEN1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ELSE
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>           MOVE PF-LEN TO P-LEN2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'OU'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 1 TO N-OUT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PF-LEN TO OUT-LEN (N-OUT).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'MD'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PD-MODE TO P-MODE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'K1'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 1 TO N-K1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PK-POS TO K1-POS (N-K1)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PK-LEN TO K1-LEN (N-K1)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD PK-LEN TO KL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'K2'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 1 TO N-K2
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PK-POS TO K2-POS (N-K2)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PK-LEN TO K2-LEN (N-K2)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD PK-LEN TO KL2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'FM'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 1 TO N-FM
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PM-IPOS TO FM-IPOS (N-FM)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PM-ILEN TO FM-ILEN (N-FM)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PM-OPOS TO FM-OPOS (N-FM)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PM-OLEN TO FM-OLEN (N-FM).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO PARM-LECT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-FIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE PARMF.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* Keys of different lengths: the shorter one is space-padded.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF KL2 > KL
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE KL2 TO KL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT FI1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT FI2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN OUTPUT FO1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF N-OUT > 1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        OPEN OUTPUT FO2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     PERFORM READ-1 THRU READ-1-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     PERFORM READ-2 THRU READ-2-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FUSION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF EOF1 = 'Y' AND EOF2 = 'Y'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO FINW.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF KEY1 (1:KL) < KEY2 (1:KL)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM READ-1 THRU READ-1-END
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO FUSION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF KEY1 (1:KL) > KEY2 (1:KL)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE 1 TO TARGET
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM WRITE-MASTER
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM READ-2 THRU READ-2-END
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO FUSION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-MODE = 'C'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE 2 TO TARGET
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM WRITE-MASTER
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM READ-2 THRU READ-2-END
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO FUSION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-MODE = 'D'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 1 TO NB-DEL
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM READ-2 THRU READ-2-END
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO FUSION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     PERFORM WRITE-UPDATED THRU WRITE-UPDATED-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-MODE = 'U'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM READ-1 THRU READ-1-END
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM READ-2 THRU READ-2-END
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO FUSION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* M (FUSBA2): the same update record serves every master with
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* this key; read file 1 when the master key moves on.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE KEY2 TO PREV-KEY2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     PERFORM READ-2 THRU READ-2-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF KEY2 (1:KL) > PREV-KEY2 (1:KL)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM READ-1 THRU READ-1-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO FUSION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => READ-1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO RECIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ FI1 INTO RECIN AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF EOF1 = 'Y'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE HIGH-VALUES TO KEY1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO READ-1-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO NB-LUS1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO REC1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE WS-LEN1 TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > P-LEN1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE P-LEN1 TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > 0
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE RECIN (1:CP-LEN) TO REC1 (1:CP-LEN).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO KEY1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO KP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO I.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => KEY1-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF I > N-K1 GO TO READ-1-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC1 (K1-POS (I):K1-LEN (I))
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>       TO KEY1 (KP:K1-LEN (I)).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD K1-LEN (I) TO KP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO I.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO KEY1-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => READ-1-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => READ-2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO RECIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ FI2 INTO RECIN AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF EOF2 = 'Y'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE HIGH-VALUES TO KEY2
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO READ-2-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO NB-LUS2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO REC2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE WS-LEN2 TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > P-LEN2
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE P-LEN2 TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > 0
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE RECIN (1:CP-LEN) TO REC2 (1:CP-LEN).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO KEY2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO KP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO I.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => KEY2-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF I > N-K2 GO TO READ-2-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC2 (K2-POS (I):K2-LEN (I))
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>       TO KEY2 (KP:K2-LEN (I)).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD K2-LEN (I) TO KP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO I.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO KEY2-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => READ-2-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => WRITE-MASTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO RECOUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC2 (1:P-LEN2) TO RECOUT (1:OUT-LEN (TARGET)).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF TARGET = 1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        WRITE FO1-REC FROM RECOUT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 1 TO NB-OUT1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ELSE
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        WRITE FO2-REC FROM RECOUT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 1 TO NB-OUT2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => WRITE-UPDATED.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO RECOUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC2 (1:P-LEN2) TO RECOUT (1:OUT-LEN (1)).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO I.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => MOVE-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF I > N-FM GO TO MOVE-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC1 (FM-IPOS (I):FM-ILEN (I))
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>       TO RECOUT (FM-OPOS (I):FM-OLEN (I)).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO I.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO MOVE-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => MOVE-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE FO1-REC FROM RECOUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO NB-OUT1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO NB-MAJ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => WRITE-UPDATED-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FINW.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE '   RECORDS READ FILE 1  ' TO DISP-MESSAGE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE NB-LUS1 TO DISP-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DISPLAY DISPLAY-LINE UPON PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE '   RECORDS READ FILE 2  ' TO DISP-MESSAGE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE NB-LUS2 TO DISP-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DISPLAY DISPLAY-LINE UPON PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE '    RECORDS WRITTEN 1   ' TO DISP-MESSAGE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE NB-OUT1 TO DISP-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DISPLAY DISPLAY-LINE UPON PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE '    RECORDS WRITTEN 2   ' TO DISP-MESSAGE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE NB-OUT2 TO DISP-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DISPLAY DISPLAY-LINE UPON PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE '    RECORDS UPDATED     ' TO DISP-MESSAGE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE NB-MAJ TO DISP-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DISPLAY DISPLAY-LINE UPON PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE '    RECORDS DELETED     ' TO DISP-MESSAGE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE NB-DEL TO DISP-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DISPLAY DISPLAY-LINE UPON PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE FI1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE FI2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE FO1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF N-OUT > 1
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        CLOSE FO2.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     STOP RUN.
</DATA>
<DATA=Documentation>
  -MAP-
  Documentation
  * SSG-4 (MT-043): one FUSBA for every FUSBA and FUSBA2 call.
  * Files, key fields, mode and field moves come from the SGSPARM
  * file written by the skeleton hand-off; see
  * _scratch\spike-fusba\spec.md. File 1 = update file, file 2 =
  * master. Modes: C split, D delete, U update, M update with
  * several masters per key (FUSBA2).
  PROGRAM-ID. .
  -MAPEND-
  -MAP-
  Technical issues
  -MAPEND-
</DATA>
<IN FOLDER>
COBOL
</IN FOLDER>
</OBJECT>
<OBJECT=ASSURFED-UTILIT-SCAN-GN,COBOL PROGRAM>
<REVDATA>
<VERSION=1.0>
<USER=>
<DATE=20090101>
<TIME=1200>
<LOCKED=False>
<DESCRIPTION=COBOL PROGRAM>
</REVDATA>
<DATA=Options>
  Name=ASSURFED-UTILIT-SCAN-GN
  Description=COBOL PROGRAM
  Parameter=
</DATA>
<DATA=Code>
  2009-01-01 12:00  => IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* SSG-4 (MT-043): one SCAN for every call. Record length, the
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* input name in the end line and the IF R < n limit come from the
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* SGSPARM file written by the skeleton hand-off; see
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* _scratch\spike-scan\spec.md. Print lines as the skeleton.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PROGRAM-ID. 'ASSURFED-UTILIT-SCAN-GN'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => CONFIGURATION SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => SOURCE-COMPUTER.  UNIVAC-1100-60EIS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => OBJECT-COMPUTER.  UNIVAC-1100-60EIS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => SPECIAL-NAMES.  PRINTER IS LISTE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE-CONTROL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT  PARMF  ASSIGN  TO  DISC SGSPARM.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT  TAPEIN  ASSIGN  TO  DISC SCANIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT  PRT  ASSIGN  TO  PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DATA DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  PARMF
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  P-TYPE         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  P-REST         PIC X(78).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-LEN-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PL-LEN         PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(73).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-NAME-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PN-TEXT        PIC X(37).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(41).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-MAX-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PX-MAX         PIC 9(10).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(68).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  TAPEIN
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD IS STANDARD
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     RECORD VARYING IN SIZE FROM 1 TO 4001
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DEPENDING ON WS-IN-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  REC-IN             PIC X(4001).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  PRT      LABEL RECORD IS OMITTED  DATA RECORD IS PRT-LINE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PRT-LINE          PIC X(100)          USAGE  DISPLAY-1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  RECIN              PIC X(4001).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  REC-AREA           PIC X(4000).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  WS-CHUNK           PIC X(100).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  WS-IN-LEN          PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  CP-LEN             PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  P-LEN              PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  P-MAX              PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  N-CHUNK            PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  K                  PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 77  KP                 PIC 9(5) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  SKIP                         PIC  9(10)  COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  LINE-CNT            PIC 9(10) COMP    VALUE 66.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  REC-IN-CT                    PIC  9(10)  COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  REC-FOUND-CT                 PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 0.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  CT-LINE                               USAGE  DISPLAY-1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER       PIC XX  VALUE '**'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 CT-CT        PIC ZZZZZZ9.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER        PIC XX   VALUE '**'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(121) VALUE SPACES.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  F-LINE  USAGE DISPLAY-1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER        PIC XX  VALUE '**'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 F-CT        PIC ZZZZZZ9.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER         PIC XX   VALUE '**'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(08) VALUE '........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '2.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '3.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '4.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '5.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '6.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '7.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '8.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '9.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '0.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '1.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(10) VALUE '2.........'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03 FILLER          PIC X(03) VALUE '3..'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  FIVE-CT PIC 9(10) COMP VALUE 6.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  M-LINE                                USAGE  DISPLAY-1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(20)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         VALUE '** END SCAN **      '.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  M-NAME         PIC X(37).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  M-CT           PIC Z(10)9.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(19)
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         VALUE  ' RECORD MATCHING = '.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FN-CT          PIC Z(10)9.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PROCEDURE DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => OPEN-FILES SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-READ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO M-NAME.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT PARMF.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-LECT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ PARMF AT END GO TO PARM-FIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'IN'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PL-LEN TO P-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'MN'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PN-TEXT TO M-NAME.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'MX'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PX-MAX TO P-MAX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO PARM-LECT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-FIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE PARMF.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     COMPUTE N-CHUNK = (P-LEN + 99) / 100.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FIRST-READ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT  TAPEIN.  OPEN OUTPUT  PRT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => LR. MOVE SPACES TO RECIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ  TAPEIN  INTO  RECIN  AT END  GO TO END-OUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO REC-AREA.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE WS-IN-LEN TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > P-LEN
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE P-LEN TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > 0
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE RECIN (1:CP-LEN) TO REC-AREA (1:CP-LEN).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO REC-IN-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => TEST-FIELDS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-MAX > 0 AND REC-IN-CT NOT < P-MAX GO TO LR.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FOUND-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD  1  TO  REC-FOUND-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE ZERO  TO  LINE-CNT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO FIVE-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF FIVE-CT > 9 MOVE REC-IN-CT TO F-CT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>       WRITE PRT-LINE FROM F-LINE AFTER 1 MOVE 1 TO FIVE-CT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>      ELSE   MOVE REC-IN-CT TO CT-CT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>       WRITE PRT-LINE FROM CT-LINE AFTER 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO LINE-CNT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  1  TO  SKIP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO K.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PRINT-CHUNK.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF K > N-CHUNK GO TO PRINT-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     COMPUTE KP = (K - 1) * 100 + 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC-AREA (KP:100) TO WS-CHUNK.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE  PRT-LINE  FROM  WS-CHUNK  AFTER ADVANCING SKIP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO LINE-CNT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO SKIP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO K.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO PRINT-CHUNK.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PRINT-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES  TO REC-AREA.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  1  TO  SKIP.     GO  TO  LR.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => END-OUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  REC-IN-CT  TO  M-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC-FOUND-CT  TO  FN-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE PRT-LINE  FROM  M-LINE AFTER ADVANCING 10 LINES.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE  TAPEIN  PRT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     STOP RUN.
</DATA>
<DATA=Documentation>
  -MAP-
  Documentation
  * SSG-4 (MT-043): one SCAN for every call. Record length, the
  * input name in the end line and the IF R < n limit come from the
  * SGSPARM file written by the skeleton hand-off; see
  * _scratch\spike-scan\spec.md. Print lines as the skeleton.
  PROGRAM-ID. .
  -MAPEND-
  -MAP-
  Technical issues
  -MAPEND-
</DATA>
<IN FOLDER>
COBOL
</IN FOLDER>
</OBJECT>
